  "report_summary": "Ultrasound of the right axilla and left chest wall performed at [redacted] on [redacted] in a patient with previously treated bilateral breast cancer and left axillary recurrence, following PET CT showing a right axillary node and suspicious left chest wall lesions. Biopsy-proven disease in the left axilla was sonographically identified. Two enhancing lesions measuring 8 mm and 9 mm were identified in the left lateral chest wall. The right axilla was extremely challenging to examine due to postsurgical change and multiple surgical clips; the CT-identified lymph node was most likely appreciated, measuring 5 mm, with multiple adjacent vessels. Ultrasound-guided core biopsy (2 cores) of the left anterior chest wall lesion was performed; the patient elected to await histology before right axillary sampling, which if required should be by FNA with cytology present. Conclusion: left breast U6 (biopsy-proven disease); right breast U3."
